# Plugin API Standards

## Objective
Maintain a consistent, powerful, and secure Plugin API that enables rich extensibility while preserving application stability and performance.

## Context
- TypeScript-based API with strong typing
- Event-driven architecture for reactive plugins
- Secure API surface with permission model
- Extensible architecture supporting multiple extension points
- Backward compatibility considerations

## Rules

### API Design Principles

#### Consistency
- **Naming conventions**: Use consistent naming across all API methods
- **Parameter patterns**: Follow consistent parameter and return patterns
- **Error handling**: Use consistent error handling approaches
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Consistent API naming
  interface DownloadAPI {
    registerDownloadSource: (source: DownloadSource) => void;
    unregisterDownloadSource: (sourceId: string) => void;
    getDownloadSources: () => DownloadSource[];
    
    onDownloadProgress: (callback: ProgressCallback) => UnsubscribeFunction;
    onDownloadComplete: (callback: CompleteCallback) => UnsubscribeFunction;
    onDownloadError: (callback: ErrorCallback) => UnsubscribeFunction;
  }
  
  ❌ // Inconsistent naming
  interface BadAPI {
    addSource: (source: DownloadSource) => void;
    removeDownloadSource: (id: string) => void;
    getSources: () => DownloadSource[];
    
    progressListener: (callback: Function) => void;
    onComplete: (cb: Function) => Function;
  }
  ```

#### Type Safety
- **Strong typing**: Provide comprehensive TypeScript types
- **Generic support**: Use generics for flexible APIs
- **Union types**: Use union types for controlled options
  ```typescript
  ✅ // Strong typing
  interface UIAPI {
    registerModal<T extends PluginModalProps>(
      config: PluginModalConfig<T>
    ): Promise<void>;
    
    showModal<T extends PluginModalResult>(
      modalId: string,
      props?: Partial<T>
    ): Promise<T | null>;
    
    addTaskbarButton(config: TaskbarButtonConfig): void;
    removeTaskbarButton(buttonId: string): void;
  }
  
  interface TaskbarButtonConfig {
    id: string;
    label: string;
    icon: IconName | React.ReactNode;
    position?: 'left' | 'right';
    tooltip?: string;
    onClick: () => void;
    visible?: boolean;
  }
  
  ❌ // Weak typing
  interface BadUIAPI {
    addButton(config: any): void;
    showDialog(id: string, data: object): Promise<any>;
  }
  ```

### Extension Points

#### Modal Extensions
- **Standard modal interface**: Consistent modal extension pattern
- **Lifecycle management**: Proper modal lifecycle handling
- **Size and positioning**: Flexible modal sizing options
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface PluginModalConfig<T extends PluginModalProps = PluginModalProps> {
    id: string;
    title: string;
    component: React.ComponentType<T>;
    size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | 'full';
    closable?: boolean;
    backdrop?: boolean;
    keyboard?: boolean;
    callbacks?: PluginModalCallbacks;
  }
  
  interface PluginModalCallbacks {
    onMount?: () => void;
    onUnmount?: () => void;
    onShow?: () => void;
    onHide?: () => void;
  }
  
  ✅ // Usage example
  api.ui.registerModal({
    id: 'plugin-settings',
    title: 'Plugin Settings',
    component: SettingsModal,
    size: 'md',
    closable: true,
    callbacks: {
      onMount: () => loadSettings(),
      onUnmount: () => saveSettings()
    }
  });
  ```

#### Taskbar Extensions
- **Button management**: Add/remove taskbar buttons
- **Visual consistency**: Maintain visual consistency with existing buttons
- **Responsive behavior**: Handle different taskbar states
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface TaskbarButtonConfig {
    id: string;
    label: string;
    icon: IconName | React.ReactNode;
    position?: 'left' | 'right';
    tooltip?: string;
    onClick: () => void;
    visible?: boolean;
    disabled?: boolean;
    badge?: string | number;
  }
  
  ✅ // Register taskbar button
  api.ui.addTaskbarButton({
    id: 'format-converter',
    label: 'Convert Format',
    icon: 'convert',
    position: 'right',
    tooltip: 'Convert download formats',
    onClick: () => openFormatConverter(),
    visible: true
  });
  
  ❌ // Minimal configuration
  api.ui.addButton({ id: 'btn', click: handler });
  ```

#### Side Panel Extensions
- **Panel registration**: Register collapsible side panels
- **State persistence**: Handle panel state persistence
- **Integration**: Seamless integration with main UI
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface PluginSidePanelConfig {
    id: string;
    title: string;
    icon?: IconName | React.ReactNode;
    component: React.ComponentType<PluginSidePanelProps>;
    position: 'left' | 'right';
    defaultWidth?: number;
    minWidth?: number;
    maxWidth?: number;
    resizable?: boolean;
    collapsible?: boolean;
    defaultCollapsed?: boolean;
    callbacks?: PluginSidePanelCallbacks;
  }
  
  ✅ // Register side panel
  api.ui.registerSidePanel({
    id: 'plugin-info',
    title: 'Plugin Information',
    icon: 'info',
    component: PluginInfoPanel,
    position: 'right',
    defaultWidth: 300,
    resizable: true,
    collapsible: true
  });
  ```

### Event System

#### Event Registration
- **Typed events**: Use strongly typed event interfaces
- **Subscription management**: Provide subscription management
- **Error handling**: Handle event errors gracefully
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface DownloadEventAPI {
    onDownloadStart(callback: (event: DownloadStartEvent) => void): UnsubscribeFunction;
    onDownloadProgress(callback: (event: DownloadProgressEvent) => void): UnsubscribeFunction;
    onDownloadComplete(callback: (event: DownloadCompleteEvent) => void): UnsubscribeFunction;
    onDownloadError(callback: (event: DownloadErrorEvent) => void): UnsubscribeFunction;
  }
  
  interface DownloadProgressEvent {
    downloadId: string;
    progress: number; // 0-100
    speed: number; // bytes per second
    eta: number; // seconds remaining
    downloadedBytes: number;
    totalBytes: number;
  }
  
  ✅ // Event subscription with cleanup
  const unsubscribe = api.downloads.onDownloadProgress((event) => {
    updateProgressDisplay(event.downloadId, event.progress);
  });
  
  // Store unsubscribe function for cleanup
  this.eventCleanupFunctions.push(unsubscribe);
  
  ❌ // No cleanup management
  api.downloads.onProgress((data) => {
    // Handle progress without storing cleanup function
  });
  ```

#### Custom Events
- **Plugin-specific events**: Allow plugins to emit custom events
- **Event namespacing**: Namespace events by plugin
- **Cross-plugin communication**: Enable secure plugin communication
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface PluginEventAPI {
    emit<T = unknown>(eventName: string, data: T): void;
    on<T = unknown>(eventName: string, callback: (data: T) => void): UnsubscribeFunction;
    off(eventName: string, callback: Function): void;
    once<T = unknown>(eventName: string, callback: (data: T) => void): void;
  }
  
  ✅ // Plugin event usage
  // Emit custom event
  api.events.emit('plugin:format-converter:conversion-complete', {
    originalFormat: 'mp4',
    targetFormat: 'mp3',
    downloadId: 'abc123'
  });
  
  // Listen for events from other plugins
  api.events.on('plugin:metadata-scraper:metadata-extracted', (data) => {
    handleMetadataUpdate(data);
  });
  ```

### Storage API

#### Plugin Data Storage
- **Isolated storage**: Each plugin gets isolated storage
- **Type-safe operations**: Provide type-safe storage operations
- **Migration support**: Support data migration between versions
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface PluginStorageAPI {
    get<T = unknown>(key: string): Promise<T | null>;
    set<T = unknown>(key: string, value: T): Promise<void>;
    delete(key: string): Promise<void>;
    clear(): Promise<void>;
    keys(): Promise<string[]>;
    
    // Bulk operations
    getMultiple<T = unknown>(keys: string[]): Promise<Array<T | null>>;
    setMultiple<T = unknown>(entries: Array<[string, T]>): Promise<void>;
  }
  
  ✅ // Type-safe storage usage
  interface PluginSettings {
    theme: 'light' | 'dark';
    autoConvert: boolean;
    defaultFormat: string;
  }
  
  const settings = await api.storage.get<PluginSettings>('settings');
  await api.storage.set('settings', {
    theme: 'dark',
    autoConvert: true,
    defaultFormat: 'mp3'
  });
  
  ❌ // Untyped storage
  const data = await api.storage.get('data'); // Unknown type
  await api.storage.set('data', someObject); // No type checking
  ```

### Format API

#### Format Registration
- **Format definitions**: Register custom download formats
- **Conversion support**: Support format conversion
- **Metadata handling**: Handle format-specific metadata
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface FormatAPI {
    registerFormat(format: DownloadFormat): void;
    unregisterFormat(formatId: string): void;
    getFormats(): DownloadFormat[];
    
    registerConverter(converter: FormatConverter): void;
    convert(fromFormat: string, toFormat: string, filePath: string): Promise<string>;
    
    getSupportedFormats(url: string): Promise<string[]>;
  }
  
  interface DownloadFormat {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    extension: string;
    mimeType: string;
    quality?: QualityOption[];
    audioCodec?: string[];
    videoCodec?: string[];
    containerFormat?: string;
  }
  
  ✅ // Register custom format
  api.formats.registerFormat({
    id: 'custom-hd',
    name: 'Custom HD',
    extension: 'mp4',
    mimeType: 'video/mp4',
    quality: [
      { id: '720p', name: '720p HD', resolution: '1280x720' },
      { id: '1080p', name: '1080p Full HD', resolution: '1920x1080' }
    ],
    videoCodec: ['h264', 'h265'],
    audioCodec: ['aac', 'mp3']
  });
  ```

### Permission System

#### Permission Declaration
- **Explicit permissions**: Require explicit permission declarations
- **Granular permissions**: Provide fine-grained permission control
- **Runtime checks**: Enforce permission checks at runtime
  ```typescript
  ✅ interface PluginPermissions {
    'downloads:read': 'Read download information';
    'downloads:write': 'Modify downloads and add new sources';
    'filesystem:read': 'Read files from the filesystem';
    'filesystem:write': 'Write files to the filesystem';
    'network:request': 'Make network requests';
    'ui:modal': 'Show modal dialogs';
    'ui:notification': 'Display notifications';
    'settings:read': 'Read application settings';
    'settings:write': 'Modify application settings';
  }
  
  ✅ // Permission checking
  async function performSecureOperation(api: PluginAPI) {
    if (!await api.permissions.hasPermission('downloads:write')) {
      throw new PluginPermissionError(
        'This operation requires downloads:write permission'
      );
    }
    
    // Proceed with operation
    await api.downloads.addDownload(downloadInfo);
  }
  
  ❌ // No permission checking
  api.downloads.addDownload(downloadInfo); // Could fail silently
  ```

## Exceptions
- **Legacy plugin support**: May require backward compatibility APIs
- **Performance optimization**: Critical paths may bypass some checks
- **Development mode**: May have additional debugging APIs
- **Platform-specific extensions**: May require platform-specific APIs

## Enforcement
- TypeScript compiler for type checking
- Runtime permission validation
- API usage monitoring and rate limiting
- Plugin lifecycle management

